-- Applied 2026-09-05, after 0002.
--
-- The 0001 seed took each post's featured image from the first <img> in its
-- body. On 215 posts that is a -1024x538 thumbnail Elementor generated, not
-- the full-size lead image the post declares as its og:image.
--
-- Nothing on the site was wrong because of it: a migrated post renders og:image
-- out of its preserved head_json, not out of featured_id. But a post written
-- through the authoring feature has no preserved head, so it would have shipped
-- a thumbnail as its social image.
--
-- The statements themselves are generated by db/fix_featured.py, which reads
-- the declared og:image out of each static page and is re-runnable. Shape:
--
--   INSERT OR IGNORE INTO media (path) VALUES ('/wp-content/uploads/...'), ...;
--   UPDATE posts SET featured_id =
--     (SELECT id FROM media WHERE path = '<the declared og:image>')
--    WHERE slug = '<slug>';
--
-- After applying: 478 posts, 0 without a featured image, and the 21 that still
-- point at a sized variant are ones whose original og:image is itself sized.
--
--   python3 db/fix_featured.py
--   npx wrangler d1 execute vinylwraptoronto-blog --remote --file=db/fix_featured.sql
